As shown in the figure, a right triangular ruler $ACB$ is rotated clockwise around vertex $B$ of the $30^{\circ}$ angle such that point $A$ coincides with point $E$ on the extension line of $CB$.

[[IMG:0]]

(1) How many degrees was the triangle ruler rotated?
(2) Connect $CD$, determine the shape of $\triangle CBD$;
(3) Find the degree measure of $\angle BDC$.

Given two points $A(-2, 1)$ and $B(-3, 0)$:
(1) Rotate $\triangle ABO$ clockwise by $90^{\circ}$ to obtain $\triangle A_{1}B_{1}O$, find the coordinates of points $A_{1}, B_{1}$;
(2) Translate $\triangle A_{1}B_{1}O$ to the right by 2 units along the x-axis to obtain $\triangle A_{2}B_{2}C$, find the coordinates of points $A_{2}, B_{2}, C$;
(3) Draw the symmetric figure of $\triangle A_{2}B_{2}C$ with respect to the origin $O$ to obtain $\triangle A_{3}B_{3}D$, find the coordinates of points $A_{3}, B_{3}, D$.

Given four points in the plane $A(0, 0)$, $B(10, 0)$, $C(10, 6)$, $D(0, 6)$, line $y = mx - 3m + 2$ divides quadrilateral $ABCD$ into two parts of equal area, then the value of $m$ is ____.

Given that a function with respect to $x$ satisfies the following three conditions simultaneously:
① The graph of the function does not pass through the second quadrant;
② When $x < 2$, the corresponding function value $y < 0$;
③ When $x < 2$, function value $y$ increases as $x$ increases.
A function analytical expression meeting these requirements can be: ____ (write any valid one).
